{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For the leader, a psalm of David — Deliver me, YHWH, from the evil man:</b> David composed this psalm before he became king, in the days of Saul, for he feared that people would inform against him to Saul. So too he says: a man of tongue." "And the word תנצרני — is complete, like: וכל עצביכם תנגושו (and all your enemies you shall trample)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 140, :notes {0 "Resolved לפני מלכו ('before his king') as 'before he became king' based on the context of the Saulide period."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:20.885443551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}